{
  "version": "0.1",
  "note": "The architecture review question bank (track B of docs/analyzers/SELF_ASSESSMENT_ROADMAP.md; explained in docs/analyzers/REVIEW_QUESTION_BANK.md). witnesses.ts computes the model witnesses; the agent resolves them by the runbook (RUNBOOK.md). Witness kinds: `present` fires when the model has none of `anyType`; `has` lists elements of `type` that have none of the `anyOf` shapes (an `otherType` ending in '.' matches any type in that layer or layer.type prefix); `trace` lists elements of `from` that no chain over `via` (at most `maxDepth` steps) connects to a `to` type; `code` is a CBM query the agent runs and compares with the model. `applies` is read from the model (`anyLayer`, `anyType`) or the code (`code`, run by the agent); a question with no `applies` always applies.",
  "decisions": {
    "intent": "The agent may propose intent elements (goals, outcomes, capabilities, personas, stakeholders) with no document naming them, staged with sourceProvenance `inferred` and the reason in the answer log (maintainer, 2026-11-21).",
    "depth": "Security and testing are asked against the full layer spec, not a subset (maintainer, 2026-11-21).",
    "overlap": "Q6 (full-stack trace) is kept beside Q4, Q5 and Q7 for the pilot; the set-cover curve decides (maintainer, 2026-11-21).",
    "p0": "The extraction re-run is a pre-pass whose cards are handed to the questions, not a question of its own (maintainer, 2026-11-21)."
  },
  "prepass": {
    "id": "P0",
    "question": "What significant code does the model not cover?",
    "how": "Run codebase_extract (tiers 0 and 1, no `since`) with the model's changesets inactive, list the element cards it stages that the model lacks, group them by layer and discard the as-built changeset. Each group goes to the question whose layers cover it; the agent records each card it adds under that question."
  },
